     "description": "The last 12 full months as recorded, then the forecast: customers you already have and customers the budget buys."
    },
    {
     "type": "forecast_cards",
     "title": "Next 12 months"
    },
    {
     "type": "forecast_assumptions",
     "title": "Baselines and assumptions",
     "description": "Every number the forecast starts from, where it comes from, and what would make it a Fact."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Data",
   "components": [
    {
     "type": "data"
    },
    {
     "type": "notes",
     "items": [
      "Customer Acquisition dates each customer by their first order, so revenue per new customer is read by months since that order.",
      "CAC is blended: ad spend over every new customer, organic ones included. A budget of zero would buy no customers in this model.",
      "Ad spend ends a few days before orders, so the window stops at the last month both cover in full."
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "improvements": [
